<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ain-i-Akbari</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ain-i-Akbari is a detailed account of the administration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, written by his minister Abu'l-Fazl and completed around 1598 as the third volume of his Akbarnama. It describes the court, army, revenue system and provinces, with statistics on crops, prices and local chiefs. It is one of the most important sources for 16th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ain-i-akbari.jpg" alt="Ain-i-Akbari" width="320" height="540" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basawan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basawan_-_The_Young_Emperor_Akbar_Arrests_the_Insolent_Shah_Abu%E2%80%99l-Maali,_page_from_a_manuscript_of_the_Akbarnama_-_1919.898_-_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
